notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T06:02:05.228Z","harness:codex","Fault simulation plan: deterministic scheduler and injected filesystem/clock/process faults drive ordinary SDK operations, with saved seeds and a minimal replay trace. Cover create/claim/update/close, structured collection changes, workspace singleton mutations, history append, index publication and N-branch merge. The oracle compares authoritative bytes, replayed state, hash integrity, claim ownership and accepted/discarded merge receipts after each operation. Simulate canceled operations at every durable boundary, repeat replays across supported runtimes, and minimize failing sequences. A smoke subset can prove instrumentation but not fleet throughput or all-field convergence."
body: "## Problem\nThe tests prove that operations work when nothing goes wrong. The product promise is that thousands of agents mutate the same workspace across branches without conflict or loss, and that every mutation survives a crash. Neither promise is currently tested against adversarial scheduling or IO failure.\n\n## Approach\nDeterministic simulation: control the sources of nondeterminism (scheduling, clock, filesystem outcomes) behind seeded injectors, enumerate schedules from a seed, and assert invariants after each. A failure yields a seed, and a seed yields an exact reproduction — which is what makes concurrency bugs fixable at all.\n\n## Invariants to assert\nHash-chain verification passes; storage integrity validation passes; no update is lost across concurrent writers; ids never collide; locks are never orphaned past their TTL; a merge of any two divergent branches converges to the same state regardless of merge order.\n\n## Known targets this should catch\nThe three recorded open races — workspace singleton read-modify-write, id reservation TOCTOU, stale-lock reclamation — are the acceptance targets. If the harness does not find them from a cold start, it is not searching hard enough.\n\n## Boundary\nNot a load benchmark: throughput measurement stays with the claim-throughput work. Not chaos in production."
